---
import PortfolioLayout from "../layouts/PortfolioLayout.astro";
---
<PortfolioLayout title="Projects" lang="en" page="projects">
<main id="main" data-screen-label="Projects · Project index"><section class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT PROJECTS</span><h1>It starts with making.</h1><p>Independent tools, open-source experiments, and the problems behind them.</p></div><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">All repositories on GitHub <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<div class="filter-bar"><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Project categories"><button data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button><button data-filter="capture" aria-pressed="false">Capture</button><button data-filter="think" aria-pressed="false">Agent workflows</button><button data-filter="make" aria-pressed="false">Create</button></div><label class="sort" for="sort">Sort<select id="sort"><option value="stars">Most stars</option><option value="name">Name A–Z</option></select></label></div>
<div class="collection"><div class="collection-main"><p class="collection-status" id="project-count" role="status">9 projects · Select to explore</p><div id="project-items">
<details class="project" id="videowipe" data-category="make" data-stars="51" data-name="VideoWipe" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/videowipe.jpg" data-image-alt="VideoWipe detection and review workspace" data-image-caption="Workspace screenshot"><summary><div><strong>VideoWipe</strong><p>Remove burned-in subtitles, watermarks, and overlays from video.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="51 stars">☆ 51</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">PYTHON · WEB UI · CLI</p><p>Burned-in subtitles and watermarks can limit how footage is reused. VideoWipe connects local detection, human review, and removal through a Python API, web interface, and CLI.</p><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/videowipe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source &amp; documentation ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="obsidian-kami" data-category="make" data-stars="7" data-name="Kami Reader" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/kami.png" data-image-alt="Kami Reader&#x27;s light Obsidian workspace" data-image-caption="Light workspace screenshot"><summary><div><strong>Kami Reader</strong><p>Bring the feel of reading on paper to Obsidian.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="7 stars">☆ 7</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">OBSIDIAN THEME · LIGHT & DARK</p><p>An Obsidian theme for sustained reading and writing. Warm paper tones, ink-blue accents, and serif text keep the focus on your notes, in both light and dark modes.</p><img src="/assets/img/projects/kami-reading.webp" alt="Kami Reader&#x27;s Obsidian reading view" width="1456" height="1600" loading="lazy"><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/obsidian-kami" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Theme &amp; installation ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="card-skill" data-category="make" data-stars="5" data-name="card-skill" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/card-skill.png" data-image-alt="Posters, covers, and whiteboards created with card-skill" data-image-caption="Selected examples"><summary><div><strong>card-skill</strong><p>Turn content into visual work, with quality checks built in.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="5 stars">☆ 5</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">CODEX + CLAUDE SKILL</p><p>Create posters, infographics, whiteboards, and reading cards from the structure of your content. Visual checks help the layout and imagery explain the ideas together.</p><img src="/assets/img/projects/card-infograph.webp" alt="An infographic created with card-skill" width="1441" height="1600" loading="lazy"><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/card-skill" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Skill &amp; examples ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="buddybar" data-category="think" data-stars="4" data-name="BuddyBar" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/buddybar.png" data-image-alt="Historical statusline artwork for BuddyBar, formerly Claude Buddy" data-image-caption="Historical artwork · Formerly Claude Buddy"><summary><div><strong>BuddyBar</strong><p>A small companion in your Claude Code statusline.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="4 stars">☆ 4</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">CLAUDE CODE PLUGIN</p><p>Long sessions with an agent need a sense of rhythm. BuddyBar adds a virtual pet to the statusline that follows your pace, offers gentle reminders, and grows as you work.</p><img src="/assets/img/projects/buddybar-demo.webp" alt="BuddyBar shown in a terminal statusline" width="1086" height="1448" loading="lazy"><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/buddybar" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Meet BuddyBar ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="clipplane" data-category="capture" data-stars="2" data-name="Clipplane" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/clipplane-store.png" data-image-alt="Clipplane capture popup in store artwork" data-image-caption="Store artwork"><summary><div><strong>Clipplane</strong><p>Keep the words that matter on your own computer first.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="2 stars">☆ 2</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">BROWSER EXTENSION · LOCAL FIRST</p><p>Send selected text to an org-mode inbox through a browser extension and local host. Keep an inspectable capture history, then choose whether to sync to Notion or flomo.</p><div class="demo"><span class="label">TRY SAVING THIS LINE</span><blockquote id="demo-quote">Good tools should put your ideas back in your hands.</blockquote><div class="saved" id="demo-saved" hidden></div><div class="demo-actions"><button id="save-quote" type="button">Save this ↗</button><button id="undo-quote" type="button" hidden>Undo save</button></div><p id="demo-status" role="status">Save the line to see how a thought is captured.</p><small>Demo only. Saved on this page until you refresh.</small></div><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/Clipplane" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Clipplane ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="tracework" data-category="capture" data-stars="2" data-name="Tracework" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/tracework.webp" data-image-alt="Tracework artwork showing work records becoming progress reports" data-image-caption="Project artwork"><summary><div><strong>Tracework</strong><p>Keep the reasons behind the changes.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="2 stars">☆ 2</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">CODEX + CLAUDE PLUGIN</p><p>Capture decisions, rejected approaches, and risk boundaries. From session records and cited decision queries to daily, weekly, and monthly reports, leave a trail that helps you reconstruct your reasoning.</p><img src="/assets/img/projects/tracework-site-crop.webp" alt="Tracework project showcase" width="1240" height="760" loading="lazy"><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/Tracework" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Tracework ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="taku" data-category="think" data-stars="1" data-name="Taku" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/taku.png" data-image-alt="Taku&#x27;s six-phase engineering workflow" data-image-caption="Workflow diagram"><summary><div><strong>Taku</strong><p>Give coding agents sound engineering habits.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="1 star">☆ 1</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">AGENT SKILLS</p><p>Turn scope, evidence, and verification into reusable habits so coding agents can keep intent clear and context manageable through complex tasks.</p><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/Taku" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Taku ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="weave" data-category="think" data-stars="0" data-name="weave" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/weave.svg" data-image-alt="weave project logo" data-image-caption="Project logo · No UI screenshot available"><summary><div><strong>weave</strong><p>Find a framework that makes sense of the question.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="0 stars">☆ 0</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">RESEARCH SKILL</p><p>Use three research paths to choose frameworks, test arguments, and compose evidence-backed long-form writing in Chinese, preserving sources, disagreements, and limits.</p><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/weave" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore weave ↗</a></div></div></details>
<details class="project" id="storyboard-prompter" data-category="make" data-stars="0" data-name="storyboard-prompter" data-image="/assets/portfolio/focus/storyboard.png" data-image-alt="A nine-panel cyberpunk storyboard example" data-image-caption="Storyboard example"><summary><div><strong>storyboard-prompter</strong><p>Use clear constraints for coherent characters and action.</p></div><span class="stars" aria-label="0 stars">☆ 0</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="project-body"><p class="tagline">CLAUDE CODE SKILL</p><p>Define constraints for panel grids, shared art direction, camera rhythm, and physical action to reduce character drift and motion errors across a storyboard.</p><img src="/assets/img/projects/storyboard-ink.webp" alt="A storyboard created with storyboard-prompter" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy"><div class="text-links"><a href="https://github.com/KKenny0/storyboard-prompter" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore the storyboard skill ↗</a></div></div></details>
</div><p class="snapshot-note">GitHub stars · Sep 24, 2026 snapshot · Not live</p></div>
